Never return on the same train|The train returns you|A man returns on the same train he left on; the train takes him back to the place he left, and the journey repeats.|MAN; CONDUCTOR; WIFE|A train with the same carriage|He liked the route|The train is keeping him on the journey|The train, the same station, the man's ticket|routine|eerie
Don't return with a ticket you didn't buy|The ticket returns you|A woman returns with a ticket she found; the ticket takes her back to the station where she found it.|WOMAN; CONDUCTOR; HUSBAND|A station with a found ticket|She thought it was hers|The ticket belongs to a passenger who died|The ticket, the station, the woman's bag|debt|eerie
# Stations and platforms
Never wait on an empty platform after midnight|The platform waits with you|A man waits on an empty platform after midnight; the platform starts waiting for him, and the train never comes.|MAN; STATION MASTER; WIFE|An empty platform with one light|He missed the last train|The platform is keeping him|The platform, the bench, the man's watch|threshold|eerie
Never sit on a bench facing the tracks|The tracks count you|A woman sits on a platform bench facing the tracks; every train that passes has someone she knows, and they wave.|WOMAN; STATION MASTER; PASSENGERS|A platform bench facing the tracks|It was the only seat|The next train is hers|The empty bench, the approaching train, the woman's hand|counting|eerie
Never ask a station master about a missing train|He shows you|A traveler asks a station master about a missing train; the station master leads him to a platform where the train is waiting, and it is empty.|TRAVELER; STATION MASTER; CONDUCTOR|A station office with a timetable|He was worried|The train is the one that crashed years ago|The platform, the empty train, the station master's hand|departure|eerie
Don't buy tea from a platform vendor who doesn't blink|The tea is his|A passenger buys tea from a vendor who never blinks; the tea tastes of ashes, and the vendor says it's his own.|PASSENGER; VENDOR; CONDUCTOR|A platform tea stall|He was cold|The vendor died on the platform|The tea, the vendor's eyes, the empty stall|debt|eerie
Never cross the tracks|The tracks cross you|A boy crosses the tracks to save time; the tracks follow him home and appear in his bedroom.|BOY; MOTHER; STATION MASTER|A railway track at dusk|He was late|The tracks are looking for another crossing|The tracks, the boy's room, the train whistle|threshold|eerie
Don't leave your luggage on the platform|It boards without you|A woman leaves her luggage on a platform; the luggage boards the train, and she is left behind.|WOMAN; PORTER; CONDUCTOR|A platform with a suitcase|She went to buy a ticket|The luggage is traveling to her destination|The platform, the departing train, the woman's hand|departure|eerie
Never read a timetable after midnight|The times are names|A man reads a station timetable after midnight; the times have turned into names, and his name is at the bottom.|MAN; STATION MASTER; WIFE|A station with a timetable board|He wanted to know the next train|The timetable is a list of the dead|The board, the man's name, the empty platform|witness|eerie
Don't wave at a train that doesn't stop|It stops next time|A woman waves at a train that doesn't stop; the next night it stops, and the conductor opens the door for her alone.|WOMAN; CONDUCTOR; HUSBAND|A platform at night|She was hoping someone would see her|The train is coming back for her|The train, the open door, the empty platform|invitation|eerie
Never sleep on a platform bench|You wake on a different platform|A man sleeps on a platform bench; he wakes on a platform in a city he has never visited, with his bag beside him.|MAN; STATION MASTER; WIFE|A platform bench at night|He was exhausted|The platform is a different station|The bench, the unfamiliar station, the man's bag|threshold|eerie
Don't say goodbye on a platform|The goodbye stays|A couple says goodbye on a platform; the goodbye stays there, and every time they return, they say it again.|COUPLE; CONDUCTOR; STATION MASTER|A platform with a departing train|They had to|The goodbye is repeating|The platform, the couple, the train|routine|sad
